    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The dynasty that overthrew the Shang in 1046 BCE and ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a> from Haojing near modern Xi'an.</li><li>It proclaimed the Mandate of Heaven: Heaven grants rule to the virtuous and withdraws it from the wicked.</li><li>It governed through regional states held by royal kinsmen, which later grew into the rival powers of the Warring States.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The He zun, a bronze vessel cast under King Cheng, contains the earliest known use of zhongguo, 'the central state', later the Chinese name for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

